# Scala 3's optional braces: `object A:` opens a template body that indentation
# closes, with no `{` or `}` anywhere. The row that seats it is
# `_indent/.offside/.slashes`, and this file is the smallest thing that cannot
# parse without it.
#
# The claim that matters is `spans template_body 8 33`: the body must start at
# the colon's own byte and end at the last member's last byte, because the
# indentation that closes it is invisible. A reader with no offside state does
# not produce a short `template_body`, it produces no `object_definition` at
# all - un-seated (`sc-r0`) this file comes back as loose `identifier` and
# `assignment_expression` leaves with no compilation unit over them.
#
# Deliberately comment-free, so that it separates the two scala rows: with the
# comment row un-seated (`sc-r4`) every claim below still holds. Written
# 2026-08-06; `research/joinery/consort/RESULT-4-clearance.md` had this row
# corpus-only and negative-worth.
roots 1
mends 0
holds object_definition
spans object_definition 0 33
holds template_body
spans template_body 8 33
